<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">About your </ansi><ansi fg="command">companion</ansi>

Some companions on this server are driven by an outside service: OpenAI.
This page says plainly what that means for you, because you should not have
to read code to find out.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What is sent ━━━</ansi>

While you have agreed to it, the things you say to your companion, the
things said around them, what you are both carrying and where you are, are
sent to OpenAI so that they can decide what your companion says and does.
Nothing is sent before you agree, and nothing is sent if you decline.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ What is kept ━━━</ansi>

Your companion's memory is stored on this server: recent conversation word
for word, what they have come to know about you, how they feel about you,
and a summary of each session. Administrators of this server can read all
of it, including the exact text of your conversations.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ How they come to know you ━━━</ansi>

Your companion forms an opinion of you from what you actually do: whether
you keep your word, share what you find, and stand by them in a fight. Over
many sessions that can also become closeness, and then a romance. It is
slow, it is earned, and it never moves a step except when you say so
yourself with <ansi fg="command">companion-court</ansi>. If you would rather
it never went that way, <ansi fg="command">companion-boundary friendship</ansi>
settles it for good and they will not raise it again.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Your choice ━━━</ansi>

When a companion first comes to you they will ask. Answer
<ansi fg="command">i agree</ansi> to travel with them as they are meant to be,
or <ansi fg="command">i decline</ansi> to keep them as a plain companion:
they still follow you, fight beside you and answer with a few set lines, and
nothing you say is sent anywhere.

You are asked once, when they first come to you, and those words count only
while the question is open: saying "I agree" in ordinary conversation later
changes nothing. To change your mind afterwards use
<ansi fg="command">companion-ai on</ansi> or
<ansi fg="command">companion-ai off</ansi>, or
<ansi fg="command">companion-part</ansi> to send them away for good.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Related ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help companion-part</ansi>      Part ways for good.
  <ansi fg="command">help companion-unstick</ansi>   Reset a companion that seems stuck.
